course: dictionary
lesson: 13149
title: Words about the future
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To foretell something is to say what will happen in the future before it happens. In stories, a wise woman might foretell a king's fate. «The old witch foretold that the prince would find a golden key.» Foretold is the past tense of foretell, so she said it before the key was found.
explain: Foretell can also mean to be a sign of something to come. «The swallows flying low foretold rain.» The swallows did not make the rain, but they showed that rain was on its way. When you meet foretell, look for a prophecy or a sign in the sentence.
explain: In real life, nobody can truly foretell the future. Scientists predict the weather using evidence, such as weather records and measurements. A prediction is a careful guess based on facts, not on magic.
fact: Foretell means to say what will happen in the future.
fact: The past tense is foretold: «The prophet foretold a great flood.»
fact: Foretell can also mean to be a sign of something to come, as in «The swallows flying low foretold rain.»
fact: Stories often have people who foretell the future, such as prophets, fortune-tellers and witches.
fact: In real life, nobody can truly foretell the future; science predicts using evidence.
exercise: «The old wizard foretold that the dragon would wake.» What does foretold mean? | Ran away very fast | *Said what would happen in the future | Painted a picture | Forgot something from long ago
exercise: What does foretell mean when it shows a sign? | To sleep all day | *To be a sign of something to come | Make a loud noise | Lost in a forest
exercise: Why do scientists predict the weather? | They use magic spells | They never look at the sky | *They use evidence, such as past weather records | They wish for sunshine
test: «The fortune-teller said she could foretell my future.» What does foretell mean here? | *To say what will happen | To dig a hole | To sing a song | To forget
test: «The dark clouds foretold a storm.» What is the clouds' job in this sentence? | *To be a sign that a storm is coming | To put out the sun | To change colour for fun | To make the storm
exam: «The prophet foretold that the king would lose his crown.» Which word means nearly the same as foretold? | Scrubbed | Forgave | Hid | *Predicted
